Modifications made in RokBot
----------------------------

1. Native Android React Native + Hermes patcher (replacing the legacy WebView shell)
   - android/release/ (patch-android.mjs, patch-android.py, delta-update.mjs):
     patches official Android React Native .xapk / .apks / .apk archives
     directly on the user's machine with 16KB page-aligned zipalign and
     APK v2/v3 signing.
   - android/patchers/: pure Node.js AXML, ARSC, XAPK/APKS merge, Pairip
     DEX/ELF neutralization, DEX/JNI injection, Hermes bytecode patching
     (recipes/*.gbp.gz), and signing modules.
   - android/companion/: lightweight Java companion runtime compiled to
     android/bin/classes2.dex, providing 6 native modal screens aligned with
     the iOS injection architecture, Keystore-encrypted pairing credentials,
     foreground SSE notifications, ShareTargetActivity, Tailcat integration,
     and OkHttp/Hermes endpoint interception.
   - android/bin/rokbot-native-base.apk and android/test-target/: minimal
     React Native test target APK and builder for offline patcher tests.
   - android/tests/ and android/adversarial/: unit, MockHost protocol,
     adversarial fuzzing/tamper, and emulator end-to-end test suites.

2. Decoupled Web client (web/client/ & web/patchers/)
   - Moved browser-side bridge modules (bridge.js, compat.js, gateway.js,
     services.js, layout.js, android.css, anchor-fallback.js, vnc-bridge.js,
     webview.js) directly into web/client/, removing the former dependency on
     the deleted Android WebView client directory.
   - Relocated shared web renderer patching helpers (output.mjs,
     renderer-patches.mjs, supported.json, zip.mjs) into web/patchers/.

3. Custom RokBot visual identity and shared release tooling
   - assets/logo/: deformed RokBot master SVG (rokbot-logo.svg), icon
     generator (generate_icons.py), manifest, and raster/desktop icon assets
     integrated into Host UI (host/server/public/rokbot-icon.png) and client
     targets.
   - ci/release-sign.mjs: shared release manifest and delta signing module.
   - Repository-wide Category-A rebranding to RokBot and
     https://github.com/hongfaqiu/rokbot, with upstream-constrained constants
     and migration bridges documented in docs/REBRAND_COMPAT.md.

Upstream modifications inherited from ProkBot Plus (2026-11-07 to 2026-11-19)
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

1. Windows x64 client
   - windows/: patcher, recipes, per-user installer source (Go), Tailcat
     network tooling and installer stub, tests. Builds from the official
     Windows 1.1.0 installer by default and from 0.71.2 as a fallback;
     inputs.mjs recognizes an input by size and SHA-256.
   - windows/tools/desktop-recipes/: generator, anchored edit list and the
     project code appended to original modules, producing the 1.1.0 recipes
     from the user's own installer. The 0.71.2 recipes are ported from the
     macOS recipes (windows/tools/port-desktop-recipes.mjs).
   - windows/patchers/desktop/original.mjs: extraction of the official
     installer, shared with the web client builder.
   - The installer tracks the files it owns, supports side-by-side migration
     of legacy installs and preserves occupied Start menu and URL entries.

2. Shared desktop client (mac/clients/desktop/)
   - Cross-platform changes shared by the macOS and Windows clients:
     platform.mjs, main.mjs, connection.mjs, settings.mjs, sounds.mjs,
     connect.css, native-provider.mjs, codex-bridge.mjs, codex-process.mjs,
     local-exec.mjs (UTF-8 command output on Windows) and attachments.mjs
     (POSIX Host image paths).
   - The 1.1.0 interfaces: per-edge RPC registration and window visibility
     events (main.mjs, local-services.mjs), dictation through the Host
     (dictation.mjs), search mapping (gateway.mjs) and startup defaults.
   - Connection lifecycle and reconnect fixes; on HTTP 401 the client checks
     /connect/status before disconnecting (gateway.mjs); settings survive
     failed saves and a damaged profile is kept under another name
     (client-persistence.mjs); the saved theme applies before first paint.
   - workspace.css and workspace-keys.cjs: wide reply tables, dialog send
     shortcuts and empty catalog-search dismissal.
   - host/runtime/host-computers.mjs, native-desktop.mjs, codex-prompt.mjs and
     host/server/desktop-capabilities.mjs: the Host recognizes Windows
     computers and withholds desktop execution from phones and browsers.

3. Web client Host integration & browser layer (web/, host/server/)
   - web/patchers/: builds a web client bundle from the user's own official
     Windows installer and uploads it to the user's own Host through the
     admin API (upload.mjs). The bundle is never committed or published.
   - web/client/: browser start-up data, native bridge, back navigation,
     keyboard, theme, notification handling, and Safari ResizeObserver shim.
   - host/server/web-client.mjs and updates in index.mjs, auth.mjs,
     proxy.mjs and push-service.mjs: bundle verification, atomic install,
     serving only to signed-in browsers, web device platform, origin-bound
     cookie sign-in, and noVNC bridge injection; host/server/public/:
     web-login.* and web-client.js.

4. Model API formats and routing
   - Anthropic Messages and OpenAI Responses adapters next to OpenAI Chat:
     host/runtime/anthropic-messages.mjs, openai-responses.mjs,
     openai-chat.mjs, model-common.mjs, model-session.mjs,
     model-policy.mjs, model-routing.mjs, model-errors.mjs,
     model-observation.mjs, config.mjs, host/server/models.mjs, index.mjs,
     public/model.js, public/locales-en.js and public/ids.js.
   - "minimal" reasoning effort, reasoning provenance tags, optional-parameter
     fallback, bounded error bodies, incremental SSE parsing, connection tests
     and auto review for all three formats.
   - Per-Bot model routes and profiles with ordered fallbacks
     (host/runtime/model-routing.mjs, contributed through upstream PR #2),
     model page, guarded manual summarization (host-summarize.mjs), threshold
     compaction and malformed function-name guard (model-rejection-guard.mjs).

5. Auto review, web and image tools
   - Auto review retries once on a malformed classification and logs failures
     (host/runtime/host-auto-review.mjs).
   - Native web tools fall back to automatic tool choice when forced tool
     calls are rejected; parallel searches succeed when one call succeeds
     (host/runtime/web-services.mjs).
   - Aspect ratios map to image sizes, and reference images use the image
     edits endpoint (host/server/media-providers.mjs, media-http.mjs,
     media-settings.mjs, host/runtime/media-services.mjs).

6. Message order and reliability
   - Messages from one model response are delivered in written order; IDs
     reused by concurrent responses run unordered
     (host/runtime/reliability/tool-order.mjs, tool-journal.mjs).
   - Immediate resends of acknowledged plain-text deliveries are blocked;
     failed post-turn memory requests do not stop the Host.

7. Linux deployment, ARM64, backup and recovery
   - host/deploy.py and host/release/: unified operator CLI for checks, setup,
     start, update, backup and recovery; build-before-stop updates; validated
     Compose mounts; exact-image recovery into new volumes (backup.py).
   - ARM64 Host build path, locked ARM runtime dependencies
     (host/release/arm-runtime/), ARM64 Tailcat and platform checks
     (platforms.py), Windows Tailcat target, and host/bench/ capacity tooling.

8. Admin tools, release engineering, tests and documentation
   - host/tools/host-admin.mjs CLI administration.
   - ci/: input checks, homepage version helpers, official channel snapshots,
     release packaging and nested archive verification.
   - Automated test suites in host/tests/, windows/tests/, mac/tests/,
     android/tests/, and web/tests/.
   - Bilingual documentation in README/README.en, docs/AI-INSTALL*,
     docs/ARCHITECTURE*, module READMEs, and SECURITY.md.

